Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 16:37:54 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] =?UTF-8?q?Mersey:=20DevTools=20debugging=20=E2=80=94?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20Mersey=20CDP=20domain,=20Sources=20integration,=20ABI=20v9?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Blink:
- Mersey protocol domain (domains/Mersey.pdl): evaluate/completions/
  getScripts, debugger commands (enable/disable/setBreakpoints/pause/
  resume/stepOver/stepInto/stepOut) and paused/resumed events. Five
  registration points incl. the hand-enumerated generated-outputs list in
  inspector/BUILD.gn (missing it fails only at link).
- InspectorMerseyAgent: bridges the engine's BLOCKING pause callout onto
  MainThreadDebugger's client message loop (same nested loop V8 uses; new
  RunNestedMessageLoopForMersey/Quit… entry points, lifecycle guard kept).
  setBreakpoints installs the debug hook itself — requiring a separate
  attach step failed silently. Typed pause snapshot: CallFrame/Scope/
  Variable; CDP 0-based ↔ engine 1-based converted at the boundary.
- MerseyScriptRunner: callable ReplTurn/ReplCompletionsJson (attribute
  shim now sits on top), Debug* wrappers over msy_context_debug_*, and a
  script registry for DevTools — inline scripts with the parser's start
  line (script_loader passes TextPosition), external graph modules
  recorded by the loader with full URL + engine spec.
- third_party/mersey: engine dylib + header refreshed to ABI v9
  (msy_context_debug_* exported).
- devtools-frontend DEPS bump: console language dropdown, Mersey-only
  completions, Sources bridge (gutter breakpoints, reveal-on-pause,
  standard step/resume buttons routed while Mersey is paused), drawer
  stack/scopes panel. See that repo's commit for details.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
